post-it: Icons don't open
symptoms:
	Icons don't open
checks:
	Desktop icons are part of the wallpaper
		shows: most icons are only a picture and do nothing when clicked; My Computer and the Recycle Bin still work
	Wallpaper is a picture of the desktop
		shows: Display Properties lists the wallpaper as "prank"
	A folder hidden in a corner holds the icons
		shows: a New Folder, mostly off the screen in the bottom right corner
software steps:
	Open the folder hidden in the corner
	Drag every icon in it onto the desktop
	Change the wallpaper in Display Properties
